      },
      "message": "fix(sim): rapid-in-stock reads the tool's footprint, not its centre\n\nLaw (d)'s column reading - the lateral rapid's a / mid / b samples and\n#96's vertical dive - now asks \"in stock and under the surface the\nearlier cuts left\" at every sample of the tool's footprint disc of\nradius r - gouge_tol (centre, 8 at half radius, 16 on the rim; the\ndisc rapids_radial and hidden_along already read), not at the centre\nalone. A dive centred just off the stock outline whose rim meets the\nstock, and a re-entry beside an earlier plunge whose far side is\nstill uncut, are now RapidInStock and block the post. acquit_by_prior\nalready reads the whole disc and is unchanged.\n\nPinned by vertical_rapids: a_dive_centred_half_a_radius_off_the_stock_wall_is_a_rapid_in_stock,\na_re_entry_beside_an_earlier_plunge_with_its_far_side_uncut_is_a_rapid_in_stock,\na_lateral_rapid_centred_off_the_stock_wall_with_its_rim_in_stock_is_a_rapid_in_stock\n(all fail on main), plus three clean cases (disc clear of the wall,\ndisc tangent within the gouge tolerance, lateral clear of the wall).\n\nFixes #106\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
