        "date": "2026-11-07T21:39:06Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): judge each footprint sample at the tip's own height\n\nPR #138 review: the footprint samples were judged at the tip plane, as\nif every tool were a square end, so a ball or bull diving beside a\nwall with its rim lifted clear of the stock was convicted. Each sample\nat radius rho is now judged at z_tip + lift(rho) against\nsurface_before (which caps at the stock top) - 0 for a square end or\ninside a bull's flat, the corner arc outside it, rho / tan(half angle)\nup a point - from the judged Cutter (Cutter::lift_at). The lift comes\nfrom Cutter::corner_r / tip_angle, not ToolGeom::nose_radius, which is\nthe turning nose and 0.0 for every mill kind.\n\nPinned by vertical_rapids:\na_ball_dive_beside_the_wall_with_its_rim_lifted_clear_is_clean,\na_bull_dive_whose_corner_lifts_clear_of_the_wall_is_clean (both fail\non the previous commit), a_ball_dive_whose_lifted_footprint_still_meets_the_stock_is_a_rapid_in_stock,\na_bull_dive_deeper_than_its_corner_lift_is_a_rapid_in_stock.\n\nFixes #106\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
