  {
    "sha": "3db8e8872895051e1dd68d84e0d6c0a3b82b629c",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDNkYjhlODg3Mjg5NTA1MWUxZGQ2OGQ4NGUwZDZjMGEzYjgyYjYyOWM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T21:47:29Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T21:47:29Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): footprint rings judged at the inner ring's lift\n\nPR #138 re-review: with samples only at the centre, half radius and\nrim, a stock edge falling between the half ring and the rim was judged\nby rim samples lifted almost a full corner, so a real dive into the\nwall read clean. The footprint is now 8 rings at d k / 8 with 2 k\npoints each (the rim's 16 scaled by radius), and a sample on ring k is\njudged at ring k - 1's lift - the lowest the tool stands over the band\nbetween them. Both the vertical-dive and the sideways readings take\nit; the module doc states the remaining bound (one ring spacing d / 8\nradially, the chord bulge angularly).\n\nThe bull pin at x 41.6 to Z 24.5 asserted a gouge and is flipped to a\nconviction (a_bull_dive_whose_corner_band_meets_the_wall_is_a_rapid_in_stock);\nnew pins a_ball_dive_with_the_wall_between_its_sample_rings_is_a_rapid_in_stock\n(ball 41.51 -> 22.5 and 42.0 -> 24.0) and\na_bull_dive_whose_flat_reaches_over_the_wall_is_a_rapid_in_stock\n(bull 42.2 -> 24.5) - all three fail on the previous commit; the ball\n42.9 -> 24.5 stays clean.\n\nFixes #106\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
